SUMMARY: Upper Clackamas Whitewater Festival
DESCRIPTION:The Upper Clackamas Whitewater Festival (UCWWF) will celebrat
 e its 40th anniversary from May 15–17\, 2026\, along the Wild and Scenic 
 Upper Clackamas River near Estacada\, Oregon – welcoming river enthusiast
 s and outdoor adventurers for a weekend of community and recreation.\n\nF
 irst launched in 1984 by the Northwest Rafters' Association\, ClackFest i
 s one of the nation’s longest-running whitewater events. Now an independe
 nt nonprofit organization\, the UCWWF remains dedicated to its core missi
 on: bringing the river community together\, promoting river safety and ed
 ucation\, fostering competition\, and preserving the festival for future 
 paddlers.\n\nClackFest is thrilled to offer a packed schedule of events f
 or kayakers\, paddle rafts\, oar frame rafts\, catarafts\, inflatable kay
 aks\, canoes\, stand up paddle boards and packrafts.\n\nIn between races\
 , attendees can connect with gear vendors\, test boats during demo sessio
 ns\, attend clinics\, and enjoy entertainment and food. A silent auction 
 and raffle will be available throughout the weekend. Whether you're compe
 ting\, spectating\, or visiting for the first time\, there's a place for 
 you at ClackFest.\n\nCamping is available on-site\, with additional lodgi
 ng options nearby in Sandy\, including the Best Western Sandy Inn\, as we
 ll as Camp Colton in Colton\, which offers a variety of accommodations su
 ch as cabins\, yurts\, campsites\, and RV spaces.
CATEGORIES:ClackFest,White-Water,Upper-Clackamas,Rafting
