SUMMARY: Prairie Fire - An American Frontier Rhapsody
DESCRIPTION:In celebrating its' 20th Season\, the Portland Choir & Orches
 tra is thrilled to announce that NY Philharmonic Orchestra's Principal an
 d Internationally known Cellist\, Carter Brey will perform on May 15 and 
 16\, 2026 at the Rolling Hills Community Church in Tualatin\, Oregon. Thi
 s is a Limited Time\, not to be missed opportunity to hear Mr. Brey as he
  joins the Portland Choir and Orchestra in an exciting performance of wel
 l-known music with new arrangements by Dan Forrest\, Mack Wilberg\, Mark 
 Hayes\, Ryan Murphy and others depicting the frontier west of America. Mr
 . Brey will also be performing some of his own compositions. The concerts
  are suitable for all ages.\n\nThere is plenty of handicap parking availa
 ble as well as wheelchair accessible seating in the concert hall located 
 in the Rolling Hills Community Church\, 3550 SW Borland Road\, Tualatin. 
 Tickets for both performances start at $20. Artisan chocolate exclusively
  developed for PCO will be available for sale at the concerts to help def
 ray the costs to produce the concert.\n\nIn addition to the musical perfo
 rmance during Saturday's Matinee the winners of the PCO Youth Musician Sc
 holarships will be announced. These scholarships\, open to students in Gr
 ades 6 - 12 are meant to help further studies or help defray the cost of 
 purchasing an instrument. Applications are still being accepted through A
 pril 27 and can be found on the PCO website http://www.musicinportland.or
 g. Those wishing to support the Youth Musician Scholarships can donate di
 rectly through the PCO website and / or come join the 3rd annual fundrais
 er Golf Classic at the Stone Creek Golf Course on Saturday\, June 27 in O
 regon City\, Oregon.
CATEGORIES:portland-choir-&-orchestra,Carter-Brey,NY-Philharmonic-Orchest
 ra,Rolling-Hills-Community-Church
