SUMMARY: Guns to Gardens Safe Disposal Event
DESCRIPTION:Description:\n\nIndividuals can bring their unwanted\, unload
 ed firearms to be dismantled during our anonymous safe surrender events. 
 At each event\, trained volunteers use specialized tools to dismantle the
  surrendered firearms on site\, ensuring they can never be used again.\n\
 nThe dismantled parts are transformed into garden tools\, a powerful symb
 ol of redemption that turns instruments of violence into tools that culti
 vate life.\n\nHow it Works:\n\nNo appointment needed\; just come to the c
 hurch parking lot\n\nArrive with your unloaded firearm(s) in the trunk of
  your car\n\nRemain in your vehicle\; you remain anonymous\n\nSkilled per
 sonnel remove your firearm(s) and confirm they’re unloaded\n\nTrained vol
 unteers use tools to dismantle your firearm(s) according to ATF guideline
 s\n\nLocal craftsmen transform donated parts into garden tools (to be mad
 e available at a later date)\n\nThank You Gift Cards:\n\nGuns to Gardens 
 PNW events are not traditional gun “buy backs\,” as the gun owners wait t
 hroughout the process and there is no transfer of firearm ownership. Once
  the gun is dismantled\, it is no longer legally a gun.\n\nWhile the Guns
  to Gardens event is not a traditional gun “buy back\,” we offer gift car
 ds to gun owners as a way to thank them for disposing of unwanted firearm
 s (while supplies last).\n\n$100 for a long gun / shotgun\n\n$200 for han
 dgun\n\n$300 for an assault rifle\n\nFor more info please visit http://gu
 nstogardenspnw.org/events or reach out to our team with any questions at 
 info@gunstogardenspnw.org mailto:info@gunstogardenspnw.org .
CATEGORIES:firearm,gun,garden,disposal
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/62191926b9407b
 526addc41f/69d970f5cef9e1612c02337c/scaled_640.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:Description: Individuals can bring their unwanted\, 
