SUMMARY: Risk/Reward Festival of New Performance
DESCRIPTION:The Risk/Reward Festival of New Performance returns to PICA J
 une 11–14\, 2026\, bringing together 15 Pacific Northwest artists across 
 four days of performances\, installations\, and one full-length solo work
 . Each evening centers on five short performances (each under 20 minutes)
  presented back-to-back in The Annex\, while installation work from three
  artists activates the warehouse throughout the night. On Thursday June 1
 1 and Sunday June 14\, solo performer Sarah K. Finn presents The Right Th
 ing To Be Doing — a lecture-performance and fungal fantasy about climate 
 doom\, complicity\, and interconnection. Saturday June 13 features two sh
 owcases from the Portland Drag Theatre Workshop (5pm and 10pm)\, presenti
 ng new theatrical works by Portland drag artists guided by Anthony Hudson
  (Carla Rossi) and Pepper Pepper. Tickets are pay-what-you-will. No one i
 s turned away for financial reasons. http://risk-reward.org
CATEGORIES:festival,performing-arts,contemporary-performance
